# Fixtures: real saved pages OUT, synthetic fixtures IN.
#
# Two independent reasons, and the second is the one that actually matters:
#  1. Size. A MakerWorld likes page is 6.7 MB and a YouTube Watch Later page is 12.7 MB. Git is
#     the wrong place for those.
#  2. PRIVACY. A real saved page is the collector's own viewing, shopping or reading history.
#     It must never enter a public repository, at any size.
#
# So `*.fixture.html` — hand-authored, invented ids and names, reproducing only the STRUCTURAL
# shapes measured on a real page — is committed and reviewable. Everything else is not.
# `fixtures/*/MANIFEST.json` records each file's sha256 and byte size; `npm run fixtures`
# verifies what is on disk and reports local-only pages as skipped rather than failing.
# See docs/FIXTURES.md.
fixtures/**/*.html
fixtures/**/*.html.gz
!fixtures/**/*.fixture.html
fixtures/**/_local/
